      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Both of these expressions are strictly valid only under the assumption of bivariate normality (Kendall and Stuart 1977; p. 250). In practice, large-sample variances for b and r are estimated by substituting observed for expected variances and covariances in Equations A1.20a,b, and by using $ (n - 2) $ in place of n in the denominator, although this latter modification is usually of trivial importance.",
